Source: boswas-compat
Section: otherosfs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Boswas OS Platform Team <os-platform@boswas.invalid>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-apparmor, python3:any
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: boswas-compat
Architecture: all
Depends: apparmor,
         bubblewrap (>= 0.8),
         python3 (>= 3.11),
         wine (>= 10.0~),
         wine64 (>= 10.0~),
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: boswas-cli
Description: Boswas OS Windows application compatibility (WinCompat)
 Runs approved Windows applications on Boswas OS with Wine, each in its own
 isolated environment:
 .
  * boswas-winapp installs, lists, launches, repairs and removes Windows
    applications; every command supports --json
  * one Wine prefix per application, never shared, never run as root
  * a bubblewrap sandbox per application: no access to the user's home
    directory, other applications, the network or devices unless the
    application's compatibility manifest grants it
  * the boswas-winapp AppArmor profile confines every Windows process
  * compatibility manifests (format v1) and a layered catalog with the
    statuses unknown, untested, experimental, tested, approved and blocked
  * device policy in /etc/boswas/compat/policy.conf
